				<section id="request-main-product-master">
					<h2>📦 Request Main Product Master</h2>
					<p>
						This module allows Admins to manage product creation requests submitted by sellers. Admins can review, approve, or reject these requests after verifying category mappings and product details.
					</p>

					<h3>🖥 Grid View Overview</h3>
					<p>The grid lists all requested products with the following columns:</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Material Type:</strong> Raw Material/Packing Material</li>
						<li><strong>Category/Sub Category</strong></li>
						<li><strong>Technical or Specification Name</strong></li>
						<li><strong>Measurement Unit</strong></li>
						<li><strong>Remark (optional)</strong></li>
						<li><strong>Status:</strong> Pending/Approved/Rejected</li>
						<li><strong>Actions:</strong> Edit | Approve | Reject</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>🛠 Step-by-Step Approval Process</h3>
					<ul>
						
						<li>Use filters to narrow the list:
						<ul>
							<li>Material Type</li>
							<li>Category / Sub Category</li>
							<li>Technical or Specification Name</li>
							<li>Status: Pending / Approved / Rejected</li>
						</ul>
						</li>
						<li>Click <strong>Edit</strong> to review product request details.</li>
						<li>Verify:
						<ul>
							<li>If the <strong>Category</strong> and <strong>Sub Category</strong> are valid and selected from dropdown.</li>
							<li>If either says <em>"Other"</em>, you need to add it first (<a href="#NewCategory">see below</a>).</li>
							<li>Check for duplicate product names or incorrect spelling.</li>
						</ul>
						</li>
						<li>If the data is valid, click <strong>Approve</strong> to add the main product master.</li>
						<li>If the data is incorrect or invalid, click <strong>Reject</strong> and enter a <em>Rejection Remark</em>.</li>
						<li>
								<h3><a href="assets/images/New/RequestProductMaster/Approve_Product.jpg" target="_blank">📸 Screenshot – Approve Product Request</a></h3>
										
								<img src="assets/images/New/RequestProductMaster/Approve_Product.jpg" alt="Approve Product Request Screenshot">
						</li>
					</ul>

					<h3 id="NewCategory">🔄 How to Approve “Other” Category/Sub Category Requests</h3>
					<p>Some products may include new categories or subcategories not yet created in the system.</p>

					<h4>Steps:</h4>
					<ul>
						<li>Check if the Category/Sub Category starts with <strong>“Other:”</strong>.</li>
						
						<li>Go to <strong><a href="#category-master" title="Navigate to the Category Master to add new categories.">Masters → Category Master</a></strong>.</li>
						<li>Click <strong>New</strong>, enter the missing <strong>Category Name</strong>, set status to Active, and Save.</li>

						<li>Next, go to<a href="#subcategory-master"> <strong>Masters → Sub Category Master</strong> </a> and add the missing subcategory under the newly added category.</li>
						<li>Return to <strong>Request Main Product Master</strong>.</li>
						<li>Click <strong>Edit</strong> on the request → now select the updated Category and Sub Category from dropdown.</li>
						<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>. The <strong>Approve</strong> button will now appear.</li>
						<li>Click <strong>Approve</strong> to finalize.</li>
						<li>
							<h3><a href="assets/images/New/RequestProductMaster/Add_NewCategory.jpg" target="_blank">📸 Screenshot – Add New Category or Sub-Category</a></h3>										
							<img src="assets/images/New/RequestProductMaster/Add_NewCategory.jpg" alt="Approve Product Request Screenshot">
						</li>
						<li>
							<h3><a href="assets/images/New/RequestProductMaster/Approve_NewCategory.jpg" target="_blank">📸 Screenshot – Approve Product Request with New Category</a></h3>
										
							<img src="assets/images/New/RequestProductMaster/Approve_NewCategory.jpg" alt="Approve Product Request Screenshot">
						</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>📌 Notes:</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>You can only approve a request when the Category and Sub Category are selected from the dropdown list (not marked as “Other”).</li>
						<li>Use <strong>Edit</strong> to clean up any input errors submitted by the seller.</li>
						<li>Always include a <strong>Rejection Remark</strong> to inform users why the request was rejected.</li>
					</ul>
								
				</section>

				<section id="category-master">
					<h2>📂 Category Master – User Manual</h2>

					<p>
						The <strong>Category Master</strong> module allows admin users to define categories under <strong>Raw Materials (RM)</strong> and <strong>Packing Materials (PM)</strong>. Categories organize products during creation, inquiry, and inquiry workflows.
					</p>

					<h3>🎯 Purpose</h3>
					<p>
						Categories group related items under a common classification, such as Solvents, Bottles, or Active Ingredients. These appear in dropdowns when creating or importing products.
					</p>

					<h3>➕ How to Add a New Category</h3>
					<ol>
						<li>Click the <strong>New</strong> button at the top-right of the screen.</li>
						<li>In the <strong>Category Information</strong> pop-up, fill in the following fields:
						<ul>
							<li>
							<strong>Material Type:</strong>
							Select either <em>Raw Material</em> or <em>Packing Material</em>.
							</li>
							<li>
							<strong>Category Name:</strong>
							Enter the unique category name (e.g., Bottle, Solvent).
							</li>
							<li>
							<strong>Is Add Common Name:</strong>
							
								Checkbox to show 'Common Name' field in Main product Master.<br>
								If Checkbox is enabled or Tick, the 'Common Name' field will be shown during new product creation under this category.
							
							</li>
							<li>
							<strong>Is Multi Trade Name:</strong>
							
								Checkbox to allow multiple trade names in seller My Product Master.<br>
								If Checkbox is checked, sellers can add multiple trade names per product when importing product under this category.
							
							</li>
							<li><strong>Status:</strong> Set to <em>Active</em> to make it usable across modules.</li>
						</ul>
						</li>
						<li>Click <strong>Save</strong> to create the category or <strong>Clear</strong> to reset the form.</li>
					</ol>

					<h3>📝 Example Entry</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Material Type:</strong> Packing Material</li>
						<li><strong>Category Name:</strong> Bottle</li>
						<li><strong>Is Add Common Name:</strong> ✔️ Enabled</li>
						<li><strong>Is Multi Trade Name:</strong> ❌ Disabled</li>
						<li><strong>Status:</strong> Active</li>
						<li>
								<h3><a href="assets/images/Category/Category.jpg" target="_blank">📸 Screenshot – Category Master</a></h3>								
								<img src="assets/images/Category/Category.jpg" alt="Request New Product Screenshot">
						</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>🔍 Viewing & Editing Categories</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Use the filters to search by Material Type or Status.</li>
						<li>Click the <strong>Edit</strong> button to update a category’s name, checkboxes, or status.</li>
						<li>Deactivated categories will not appear in dropdowns during product creation.</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>📌 Note:</h3>
					<ul>
						 <li>Only <strong>Active</strong> categories appear in the dropdowns on related forms like “My Product Master” and “Inquiry”.</li>
    					<li>Status change (to Deactive) will hide the category from future use without deleting existing records.</li>
											
					</ul>
				</section>

		
				<section id="subcategory-master">
					<h2>📂 Sub Category Master</h2>
					
					<h4>➕ Step to Add New Subcategory</h4>
					<ul>
						<li>Navigate to Masters → Subcategory Master.</li>
					  	<li>Fill the following mandatory fields in the popup form:
							<ul>
								<li><strong>Material Type:</strong> Choose "Packing Material" or "Raw Material".</li>
								<li><strong>Category:</strong> Select the main category from the dropdown (e.g., Bottle).</li>
								<li><strong>Sub Category Name:</strong> Enter a unique name (e.g., Pet Bottle).</li>
								<li><strong>Status:</strong> Choose Active or Deactive.</li>
							</ul>
						</li>
						<li>Click <strong>Save</strong> to create the new entry.</li>
						<li>
							<h3><a href="assets/images/Category/SubCategory.jpg" target="_blank">📸 Screenshot – Sub-Category</a></h3>							
							<img src="assets/images/Category/SubCategory.jpg" alt="Add New Sub-Category">
						</li>
					</ul>


			 		<h4>✏️ Edit Sub Category</h4>
					<ul>
						<li>Click the <strong>Edit</strong> button from the list next to the sub-category.</li>
						<li>Update the name or change the status.</li>
						<li>Save your changes.</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>📌 Important Notes</h3>
					<ul>
							
						<li>Inactive sub categories are not shown during product creation by sellers.</li>
						<li>Ensure correct mapping between Material Type, Category, and Sub Category.</li>
    					<li>Inactive sub-categories are excluded from inquiry forms or dropdowns.</li>
					</ul>
