						<section id="AutoInquiry_ReplyMaster">
							<h2> Auto Inquiry Reply Master</h2>
							<p>The <strong>Auto Inquiry Reply Master</strong> allows sellers to pre-configure automatic responses to purchaser inquiries with trade-level precision.</p>

							<h3>🎯 Purpose</h3>
							<p>This module helps streamline repetitive replies by automatically sharing offer details such as price, delivery timeline, packing details, etc., based on configured trade-level data.</p>

							<h3>📌 Steps to Use:</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Navigate to <strong>Masters ➝ Auto Inquiry Reply Master</strong>.</li>
								<li>Use filters at the top to narrow down by Material Type, RM/PM Name, Category, Trade Name, etc.</li>
								<li>Locate the desired <strong>Trade Information</strong> row to edit.</li>
								<li>Enter/update the following fields:
								<ul>
									<li><strong>Offer Price</strong></li>
									<li><strong>Price Valid Upto (Days)</strong></li>
									<li><strong>Delivery Time (Days)</strong></li>
									<li><strong>Is Negotiable?</strong> – Yes / No</li>
									<li><strong>Purity (%)</strong> (optional for Technical)</li>
									<li><strong>Warehouse</strong> – Select warehouse location</li>
									<li><strong>Packing Info:</strong> Size, Measure (e.g., ml/kg), and Type (e.g., Box, Bottle)</li>
									<li><strong>Remark</strong> – Optional notes</li>
								</ul>
								</li>
								<li>Use the <strong>Auto Reply toggle</strong> (green = enabled, red = disabled) to activate/deactivate automatic replies.</li>
								<li>Click <strong>Save All</strong> to apply changes across rows.</li>
								<li>
										<h3><a href="assets/images/AutoInquiryReplyMaster.jpg" target="_blank">📸 Screenshot – Auto Inquiry Reply Master Screen</a></h3>											
										<img src="assets/images/AutoInquiryReplyMaster.jpg"  alt="Request New Product Screenshot">									
								</li>
							</ul>

							<h3>🕓 View Auto Reply Change History</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Click the <strong>History</strong> button beside a trade entry to view a full log of changes.</li>
								<li>It shows:
								<ul>
									<li>Offer Price, Validity Days, Delivery Days</li>
									<li>Purity, Warehouse, Packing Info</li>
									<li>Is Auto Reply On/Off</li>
									<li>Updated By and Date-Time</li>
								</ul>
								</li>
								<li>
									<h3><a href="assets/images/History_AutoReplyMaster.jpg" target="_blank">📸 Screenshot – Auto Reply History Screen</a></h3>											
									<img src="assets/images/History_AutoReplyMaster.jpg"  alt="Auto Reply History Screen">									
								</li>
							</ul>
													
						</section>
						
				
						<section id="warehouse-location">
							<h2>🏬 Warehouse Location Management</h2>

							<p>
								The <strong>Warehouse Location</strong> module allows Sellers to define storage points from which materials (RM/PM) are dispatched. These locations appear in seller inquiry replies, auto-replies, and purchase orders for tracking.
							</p>

							<h3>📌 Purpose</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Used during inquiry reply and final deal confirmation</li>
								<li>Links a product or seller with a physical location</li>
								<li>Visible to purchasers on inquiry screens and PO generation</li>
							</ul>							

							<h3>📥 Add New Warehouse Location</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Go to <strong>Masters → Warehouse</strong>.</li>
								<li>Click the <strong>New</strong> button.</li>
								<li>Fill in the fullowing fields:
								<ul>
									<li>Warehouse Name</li>
									<li>GST Number</strong></li>
									<li>Address</strong></li>
									<li>State</strong></li>
									<li>District</strong></li>
									<li>City</strong></li>
									<li>Pin Code</strong></li>
									<li>Status</strong> (Active/Inactive)</li>
								</ul>
								</li>
								<li>Click <strong>Save</strong> to submit.</li>
								<li>
									<h3><a href="assets/images/SellerInquiry/MyProduct/warehouselocation.jpg" target="_blank"> Screenshot – Warehouse Location Form</a></h3>								
									<img src="assets/images/SellerInquiry/MyProduct/warehouselocation.jpg" alt="Warehouse Location Entry Form">
								</li>
							</ul>

							<h3>📋 Warehouse List/Grid</h3>
							<p>
								The grid shows a list of added warehouse locations with the fullowing culumns:
							</p>
							<ul>
								<li>Warehouse Name</li>
								<li>Full Address</li>
								<li>City, District, State, Pincode</li>
								<li>Status (Active / Inactive)</li>
								
							</ul>

							<h3>✏️ Edit or Update Warehouse Info</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Click <strong>Edit</strong> next to the warehouse.</li>
								<li>Update any field as needed (e.g. city, address, pin).</li>
								<li>Click <strong>Save</strong> to apply changes.</li>
							</ul>

							<h3>📦 Warehouse in Inquiry Flow</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Sellers must select one warehouse location per product during inquiry response or auto-reply setup.</li>
								<li>Buyers will see this dispatch location when viewing seller quotes or generating PO.</li>
								
							</ul>

							<h3>⚠️ Validations & Tips</h3>
							<ul>						
								<li><strong>Active status</strong> is required to show warehouse in seller flows</li>
								<li><strong>Duplicate warehouse names</strong> should be avoided</li>
							</ul>					
						</section>


					</section>

